To enable your BGP neighbor clusters to handle unexpected error messages without dropping sessions during polite reboots, apply the following configuration to the BGP group:

```
/configure router bgp group <group-name>
    graceful-restart
    error-handling
        update-fault-tolerance
    exit
```

### Explanation:
- **`graceful-restart`**: Ensures sessions are maintained during polite reboots by enabling BGP graceful restart helper procedures.
- **`update-fault-tolerance`**: Under the `error-handling` context, this command treats UPDATE message errors non-disruptively (e.g., using "treat-as-withdraw") instead of tearing down sessions.

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name. This configuration applies to all neighbors in the group.
