To achieve BGP path selection based on the lowest total internal cost across your network and partner networks, enable AIGP support on BGP sessions with external partners. This ensures BGP considers the end-to-end IGP metrics in path selection, even across multiple ASes.

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <PARTNER_GROUP_NAME>
        aigp
    exit
exit
```

**Replace `<PARTNER_GROUP_NAME>`** with your BGP peer group name for external partners. If configuring individual neighbors instead of a group:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <PARTNER_GROUP_NAME>
        neighbor <PARTNER_IP>
            aigp
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key Notes**:
- Partners must also support AIGP and propagate the attribute.
- AIGP accumulates IGP metrics (e.g., OSPF/IS-IS costs) across all participating networks.
- BGP path selection will prefer routes with the lowest total AIGP metric.
