To make BGP sessions more resilient to brief physical link disruptions on your Nokia 7750 SR, use the following configuration to disable immediate session teardown:

```cli
configure router bgp 
    disable-fast-external-failover 
exit
```

### Key details:
1. **`disable-fast-external-failover`** forces BGP to wait for the negotiated hold timer (default 90 seconds) to expire before declaring a peer down. This buffers against short link flaps (<90s) that would otherwise instantly kill sessions.

2. **Effect**: During a fiber blip, BGP will:
   - Retain the session while the physical layer recovers
   - Only tear down if the outage exceeds the hold-time
   - Automatically recover when connectivity resumes within the hold window

### Verification:
Confirm with:
```cli
show router bgp summary
```
