To advertise alternate labeled IPv6 paths via BGP while preserving primary forwarding, configure the add-paths capability for labeled-unicast IPv6 routes:

```console
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        label-ipv6 send 2
    exit
exit
```

**Key details:**
1. `label-ipv6 send 2` enables advertising up to 2 paths per prefix (primary + one alternate)
2. Applies to labeled-unicast IPv6 routes (MPLS labels included)
3. Local best-path selection remains unchanged (primary forwarding unaffected)
4. Actual path advertisement depends on neighbor capability negotiation

For neighbor-specific implementation, apply under the relevant group/neighbor context:
```console
configure router bgp group "GROUP_NAME" neighbor "IP_ADDRESS"
    add-paths
        label-ipv6 send 2
    exit
exit
```
