To configure your BGP setup for flaky peers with the specified backoff behavior, use the following command:

```router bgp
damp-peer-oscillations idle-hold-time 10 10 120 error-interval 45
```

**Explanation of parameters:**
- `idle-hold-time 10`: Initial cooldown after the first failure (10 minutes).
- `10`: Backoff multiplier (doubles wait time after subsequent failures: 20min, 40min, etc.).
- `120`: Maximum idle time cap (2 hours/120 minutes).
- `error-interval 45`: Stable period required to reset penalties (45 minutes).

Apply this at the appropriate BGP hierarchy level (global, group, or neighbor) based on your peer scope. The configuration implements exponential backoff starting at 10 minutes, doubling after each failure, while capping at 120 minutes and requiring 45 minutes of stability to clear penalties.
