To address the issue of VPNv4 and VPNv6 routes not resolving their next-hops due to lack of VPRN service import, configure the following:

```
configure router bgp
   enable-rr-vpn-forwarding
   next-hop-resolution
      labeled-routes
         transport-tunnel
            family vpn-ipv4
               resolution any
            exit
            family vpn-ipv6
               resolution any
            exit
         exit
      exit
   exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `enable-rr-vpn-forwarding` imports all received VPN-IP routes into a dummy VRF for next-hop resolution, regardless of route targets.  
- Under `labeled-routes > transport-tunnel`, the `resolution any` setting for both `vpn-ipv4` and `vpn-ipv6` families allows all available tunnels (RSVP, LDP, SR, etc.) to resolve next-hops.  

This ensures BGP processes the routes and populates valid forwarding information in the tunnel table.
