To enforce BGP to use only routes with MPLS info containing your custom identifier for next-hop reachability and prevent fallback to unlabeled paths, configure a next-hop resolution policy that matches labeled routes with your specific tag:

```cli
/configure router policy-options
begin
policy-statement NEXTHOP-POLICY
    entry 10
        from
            tag <custom-tag-value>   # Replace with your custom identifier
            protocol mpls
        action accept
    exit
    default-action reject
exit
commit
```

Then apply this policy to BGP next-hop resolution:

```cli
/configure router bgp
next-hop-resolution
    policy NEXTHOP-POLICY
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Creates a policy `NEXTHOP-POLICY` that only accepts MPLS routes tagged with your custom identifier
2. Explicitly rejects all other routes (including unlabeled paths)
3. Enforces the policy in BGP next-hop resolution to strictly use only tagged MPLS routes

Replace `<custom-tag-value>` with your actual tag identifier. The router will now only resolve next-hops using labeled paths carrying your specific tag.
