To hide your true ASN 65535 and backbone AS details from the BGP peer, configure the neighbor with a virtual AS and enable AS path manipulation:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "HIDDEN_AS_GROUP"
        neighbor <peer_IP>
            local-as 65001 private no-prepend-global-as
            next-hop-self
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `local-as 65001`: Presents virtual AS 65001 to the peer instead of your real AS 65535
- `private`: Removes the virtual AS 65001 from the AS_PATH in outbound updates
- `no-prepend-global-as`: Prevents your real ASN 65535 from being added to the AS_PATH
- `next-hop-self`: Ensures internal next-hop addresses aren't leaked (recommended when hiding AS details)

Replace `<peer_IP>` with the peer's actual IP address and adjust `65001` to your chosen virtual AS number. The peer will only see their own AS in received paths.
