policy-statement "EXPORT_FILTER"
    entry 10
        from community "CUSTOM_TAG_1"
        action reject
    exit
    entry 20
        from community "CUSTOM_TAG_2"
        action reject
    exit
    default-action accept
exit
commit
```

2. **Apply the policy as an export filter to your BGP peer:**
```
/configure router bgp
group "PEER_GROUP"
    neighbor <PEER_IP>
        export "EXPORT_FILTER"
    exit
exit
```

Replace `CUSTOM_TAG_1/2` with your actual community names, `target:12345:1/2` with your custom tag values, `PEER_GROUP` with your BGP group name, and `<PEER_IP>` with the neighbor's IP address.

This configuration will:
1. Create community definitions matching your custom route tags
2. Build a policy that rejects routes containing these tags
3. Apply the filter to outgoing advertisements for the specified peer

Routes containing either `CUSTOM_TAG_1` or `CUSTOM_TAG_2` communities will be blocked from being advertised, while all other routes will be permitted by default.
