To enforce a 5-minute (300-second) stale timer override for all route types from a BGP peer, configure the following command:

```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-ip> graceful-restart long-lived helper-override-stale-time 300
```

**Explanation:**  
This command overrides the peer's advertised LLGR stale-time with your locally configured 300-second (5-minute) value. It applies to all AFI/SAFI route types supported by the neighbor, ignoring their proposed timers during network disruptions.

**Replace placeholders:**  
- `<group-name>`: BGP peer group name  
- `<neighbor-ip>`: Peer IP address  

**Note:**  
- The override takes effect immediately for existing and new sessions.  
- Ensure graceful restart and long-lived capabilities are already negotiated with the peer.  
- Use `show router bgp neighbor <ip-address> family` to verify supported route types.
