Based on your request to adjust BGP keepalive intervals to 60 seconds for troubleshooting flapping sessions on your 7750 SR, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp 
    group <your-group-name> 
        neighbor <peer-IP-address> 
            hold-time 180
            keepalive 60
```

### Key points:
1. `hold-time 180` sets the session timeout to 180 seconds
2. `keepalive 60` sends keepalives every 60 seconds
3. These commands must be applied per neighbor or group
4. Ensure the peer's hold-time is at least 180 seconds for compatibility

The configured keepalive interval (60s) must be less than or equal to one-third of the hold-time (180s) to maintain session stability. Adjust these values consistently across peers to resolve flapping issues.
