To configure the Nokia 7750 SR to prefer BGP paths with higher-capacity link bandwidth metrics for traffic steering, set up the following BGP group configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "your-group-name"
        cluster <cluster-id> orr-location <location-id>
        link-bandwidth
            aggregate-used-paths ipv4
```

**Explanation:**  
- **`cluster <cluster-id> orr-location <location-id>`**  
  Enables Optimal Route Reflection (ORR) for the specified location. This ensures routes advertised to clients in this cluster are optimized based on link-bandwidth metrics. Replace `<cluster-id>` with your cluster identifier (e.g., `1.2.3.4`) and `<location-id>` with the ORR location index (e.g., `5`).  

- **`link-bandwidth`**  
  Enters the configuration context to process BGP link-bandwidth extended communities.  

- **`aggregate-used-paths ipv4`**  
  Aggregates bandwidth metrics from multipaths for IPv4 routes. This allows the router to advertise routes with a total bandwidth value representing higher-capacity links when re-advertising with `next-hop-self`.  

**Notes:**  
1. This configuration assumes the BGP peers advertise routes with `link-bandwidth` extended communities.  
2. Replace `"your-group-name"` with your BGP peer group name.  
3. Use the `allow-local-fallback` option in the `cluster` command if fallback to local topology routes is needed when no ORR-optimized paths exist.
