## User question:
On a Nokia 7750 SR, when setting up BGP monitoring tools, the routes that the router generates itself (like the ones it creates locally for interfaces or services) aren’t showing up in the reports sent to the BMP collector. How do I fix this so the box starts including those self-originated paths in its updates to the monitoring station?
---
## Proposed answer:
To ensure self-originated routes are included in BMP reports, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure
bmp
    station "station-name"
        report-local-routes
    exit
exit
```

Replace `"station-name"` with your actual BMP station name. This command explicitly enables the reporting of locally generated routes to the specified monitoring station.
