To configure BGP-originated tunnels with extra MPLS labels for improved traffic distribution and load-balancing in a multi-hop setup, use the following CLI commands:

```console
configure router
    bgp
        ibgp-multipath
        next-hop-resolution
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family ipv4 resolution any
                    family ipv6 resolution any
                exit
            exit
        exit
        best-path-selection
            ebgp-ibgp-equal label-ipv4 label-ipv6 vpn-ipv4 vpn-ipv6
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `ibgp-multipath` enables load balancing across multiple iBGP paths.  
- `transport-tunnel` with `resolution any` ensures BGP uses all available tunnel types (RSVP, LDP, SR) to resolve next-hops, adding diverse MPLS labels.  
- `ebgp-ibgp-equal` allows equal treatment of eBGP/iBGP paths for labeled and VPN routes, preventing path polarization by distributing traffic across all valid paths.  

This configuration maximizes entropy in MPLS label stacks, enhancing load-balancing efficiency for deep packet inspection.
