To set the BGP next-hop to your router's own interface IP for a specific peer, apply the `next-hop-self` command under that neighbor's configuration. Replace `<group-name>` with the BGP group name and `<peer-IP>` with the peer's IP address:

```console
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            neighbor <peer-IP>
                next-hop-self
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This ensures routes advertised to this peer use your local BGP interface IP as the next-hop, while other peers and route propagation remain unaffected.
