To adjust the TCP keepalive checks to every 30 seconds and prevent premature session drops on unstable links, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure bmp station <station-name> connection tcp-keepalive
    keep-idle 30
    keep-count 10
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `keep-idle 30` sets the initial TCP keepalive probe to 30 seconds (half a minute).  
- `keep-count 10` increases the missed probe tolerance to 10 (default is 4), preventing the router from dropping the session too quickly during instability.  

Replace `<station-name>` with your BMP station name. This configuration balances frequent liveliness checks with resilience to transient link issues.
