To configure BGP to automatically set the MED using OSPF/IS-IS IGP metrics on a Nokia 7750 SR, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router policy-options
    begin
    policy-statement "set-med-from-igp"
        entry 10
            from protocol [ospf isis]
            action accept
                metric set metric
            exit
        exit
        entry 20
            from protocol bgp
            action accept
                metric set next-hop metric
            exit
        exit
    commit
    exit

configure router bgp
    group "eBGP_Group"
        family ipv4
        export "set-med-from-igp"
    exit
```

### Key points:
1. The policy `set-med-from-igp` sets the MED based on:
   - Original IGP metric for locally originated OSPF/IS-IS routes (entry 10)
   - IGP cost to the next-hop for BGP-learned routes (entry 20)
2. Apply this policy as an **export policy** to your eBGP neighbor group using `export "set-med-from-igp"`.

### Verification:
After applying, check BGP updates with:
```cli
show router bgp neighbor <ip> advertised-routes
```
Look for the `MED` field matching your IGP metrics. Neighboring ASes will now prefer paths based on your IGP costs.
