To prioritize certain BGP routes internally by setting their metric to 200, configure the BGP local-preference attribute at the appropriate level (global BGP, group, or neighbor). Use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    local-preference 200
exit
```

Alternatively, apply it to a specific BGP group:
```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        local-preference 200
    exit
exit
```

Or apply it to a specific neighbor:
```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            local-preference 200
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` and `<ip-address>` with your specific group and neighbor details. This configuration ensures routes from the specified scope are prioritized with a local-preference value of 200.
