To configure BGP peer tracking with the specified policy "core-routes" on your Nokia 7750 SR, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    enable-peer-tracking
    peer-tracking-policy "core-routes"
exit
```

**Key points:**
1. `enable-peer-tracking` activates immediate session teardown when the route to the peer becomes invalid.
2. `peer-tracking-policy "core-routes"` links the session state to routes matching your "core-routes" policy:
   - Sessions stay up only if the route to the peer is accepted by "core-routes"
   - Sessions drop immediately if the route is rejected by "core-routes" or disappears
   - "core-routes" must be defined in `config>router>policy-options`

For neighbor-specific application, enable tracking at the group/neighbor level:
```
configure router bgp
    peer-tracking-policy "core-routes"
    group "PEER_GROUP"
        enable-peer-tracking
        neighbor 192.0.2.1
            enable-peer-tracking
        exit
    exit
exit
```
